Our only modification part is that, if the Software (or any derivative works
thereof) is used for any of your commercial products or services that have
more than 50,000 US dollars (or the equivalent in other currencies) in monthly
revenue, you shall prominently display "Wative" on the user interface of such
product or service.

For the purpose of the paragraph above:

  a. "Monthly revenue" is measured per product or service, meaning the gross
     revenue that the individual product or service incorporating the Software
     generates in a calendar month — not the total revenue of the entity
     operating it. An entity operating several products need only attribute
     those products that individually cross the threshold.

  b. "Prominently display" means the "Wative" label is visible to an ordinary
     user in the normal course of using the product or service, without
     requiring that user to open a settings pane, an "About" dialog, a licenses
     screen, source code, or documentation. Placement, size and styling are
     otherwise at your discretion.

  c. For a product or service with no user interface — a backend service, an
     API, a library, or a command-line tool — the requirement is satisfied by
     displaying "Wative" in the product's public documentation, in its startup
     or version output, or on an equivalent surface its users routinely see.

  d. The obligation applies only while the product or service remains above the
     threshold, and takes effect from the start of the calendar month following
     the month in which the threshold is first crossed.

  e. This requirement grants no other right in any trademark, service mark, or
     logo of the copyright holder, and does not permit you to state or imply
     that your product or service is endorsed by, affiliated with, or produced
     by the copyright holder.

